  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Peaceful and resilient borderlands, Democratic Republic of the Congoc of Uganda</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The borderlands between the Democratic Republic of Congo (DRC) and Uganda are characterized by porous borders, long standing cross border mobility around Lake Albert, and complex socio political dynamics shaped by conflict and colonial legacies. Insecurity on the DRC side is driven by weak border governance, competition over land and resources, illicit mining and gold trade, and armed group recruitment, resulting in recurrent displacement, limited services, and poor economic opportunities. Despite strong potential for cross border trade, development is constrained by weak infrastructure, inter community tensions, corruption, and widespread informal and illicit activities, including smuggling and human trafficking. The proposed project seeks to enhance social cohesion, security, and resilience in the DRC-Uganda borderlands by strengthening local governance, improving access to basic services, and expanding sustainable economic opportunities. The action aligns with national priorities, UN cooperation frameworks, and key regional and global commitments, including Agenda 2063, African Continental Free Trade Area (AfCFTA), EU peace and security priorities, the SDGs, and the Global Compact for Migration.</narrative>
  </description>
